Problem Statement :  

Brand Guardian: Automated End-to-End Azure Multimodal Compliance Orchestration Engine using LangGraph and LangSmith
Background & Industry Context
Digital advertising across platforms like YouTube relies heavily on short video commercials and influencer endorsements
. Advertisers and content creators are legally obligated to strictly comply with regulatory frameworks—such as FTC Disclosure Guidelines regarding sponsored endorsements
 and YouTube Ad Specifications
Currently, compliance auditing of video ads is performed manually
. Human auditors must watch every advertisement, read on-screen fine print, listen to spoken audio claims, compare them line-by-line against legal handbooks, and flag violations
. This process is expensive, time-consuming, and difficult to scale
To solve this, organizations require an automated, production-grade LLMOps Multimodal Compliance Engine
 that ingests raw video content, extracts spoken audio and visual text, performs vector-based legal policy retrieval, evaluates compliance using an LLM agent, and produces structured audit verdicts


Capstone Problem Statement
"Design, build, and deploy an end-to-end, production-grade multimodal compliance auditing pipeline on Microsoft Azure
. Given a YouTube video ad URL
, the system must automatically ingest the video, extract both spoken transcripts and on-screen visual claims (OCR)
, retrieve relevant legal and platform compliance rules from a vector knowledge base
, orchestrate a stateful agentic audit using LangGraph and GPT-4o
, and generate a structured audit report (Pass/Fail verdict with categorized severity issues)
, backed by full application monitoring and agent tracing
System Architecture & Key Technical Requirements
Participants must implement the project across five core layers
:
[YouTube URL] ──► [FastAPI Backend] ──► [yt-dlp Downloader] ──► [Azure Blob Storage]
                                                                     │
                                                                     ▼
[Pass/Fail Verdict & Report] ◄── [LangGraph Agent] ◄── [Azure AI Video Indexer]
          │                             │                 (Transcript & OCR)
          ▼                             ▼
[LangSmith & App Insights]    [Azure AI Search RAG]
 (Observability & Tracing)    (FTC & YouTube PDFs)

  
1. Entry Point & Backend Services
FastAPI Server (server.py): Expose a REST API with a POST /audit endpoint accepting video URLs and a GET /health status check
.
Pydantic Validation: Enforce strict request and response schemas (AuditRequest, ComplianceIssue, AuditResponse)
.
2. Multimodal Video Processing Pipeline
Video Ingestion: Script using yt-dlp to download YouTube video streams locally into temporary MP4 files
.
Unstructured Holding: Temporarily host raw video files in Azure Blob Storage
.
Multimodal Extraction: Integration with Azure AI Video Indexer using computer vision and speech processing to automatically extract Spoken Transcript: Full speech-to-text dialogue
.
Visual On-Screen Text (OCR): Brand claims, fine print, text disclaimers, and logos visible on video frames
.
Video Metadata: Technical properties such as video duration and platform specs


3. Regulatory Vector Knowledge Base (RAG)
Document Chunking & Vectorization (index_documents.py): Chunk regulatory PDF handbooks (e.g., FTC Guidelines and YouTube Ad Specs)
 using RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter (chunk size: 1000, overlap: 200)
.
Vector Store: Upload document vectors into Azure AI Search using text-embedding-3-small embeddings
.
Hybrid Search Retrieval: Execute hybrid vector and keyword search queries against Azure AI Search to retrieve the top-3 most relevant legal rulebook sections matching the video's transcript and OCR content

  
4. Stateful Agentic Orchestration (LangGraph)
Graph State (state.py): Define VideoAuditState using TypedDict and Annotated lists with operator.add to pass context and accumulate detected compliance issues across nodes
.
Indexer Node (IndexerNode): Manages downloading, video indexing polling loops, and structured output parsing
.
Compliance Auditor Node (ComplianceAuditorNode): Integrates Azure OpenAI (GPT-4o)
, formats system context with retrieved legal rules
, evaluates claims against guidelines, cleans markdown formatting using regex
, and outputs a strict JSON payload
.
5. Observability, Telemetry & Tracing
Azure Application Insights (telemetry.py): Configure OpenTelemetry instrumentation to track API latency, HTTP calls, database/search requests, and generate visual Application Maps
.
LangSmith: Enable tracing for the agentic graph execution to monitor prompt payloads, token usage, LLM thought chains, and node execution times





